Based on the stack‐trace and the repro, the problem is that in Group.jsx you are doing a direct children.map(…) on whatever React passed you. As soon as you have any stray whitespace/text‐nodes in your JSX, children is no longer a clean array of elements and you end up calling child.props on a string (or children.map isn’t even a function).

The fix is to switch to React.Children.map (which normalises single child, array, text, etc) and to skip non‐elements. You’ll also need to pull in Children from React’s API. Below are two small *SEARCH/REPLACE* edits for src/menu/view/group.jsx:

